# FreshLoop AI — Cursor rules

## Architecture
- Monolithic Next.js App Router. Routes live under `app/`; business logic under `lib/domains/*`.
- Keep `app/api/**/route.ts` thin: parse request → call domain → JSON response.
- Do not add new dependencies on `lib/legacy/*` or in-memory demo data.
- Canonical inventory truth: Prisma `InventoryTransaction` via `lib/domains/inventory/ledger.ts` and `stock.ts`.
- Database client: import `prisma` from `@/lib/db/prisma` (re-export from ledger is OK for compatibility).

## File layout
- UI: `components/features/<area>/`, kit: `components/ui/`, shell: `components/layout/`.
- Shared types: `@/types`. Domain imports: `@/lib/domains/...`.

## Auth & API
- Middleware requires login on `/api/*` except `/api/auth/*`, `/api/health`, `/api/pos/webhook`.
- Every mutating handler must call `requireSessionUser()` and role helpers from `lib/auth/guardRoute.ts`.
- Never trust `staffId` or `role` from JSON bodies.
- Prefer `apiErrorFromUnknown` from `lib/domains/ai/apiError.ts` for consistent errors.

## Waste KPI
- Waste % = (discard $ + volumetric scrap $) ÷ gross POS sales; use `scrapBucketEconomics` + `calculateRealTimeWastePct`.
- Admin stats merge via `getAdminStoreStatsBundle()` — do not duplicate waste math in `storeStats`.
- Default KPI window: `DEFAULT_KPI_LOOKBACK_DAYS` in `wasteKpi.ts`.

## Quality
- Match existing naming and patterns; minimal diffs.
- Run `npm run typecheck` and `npm run test` before pushing.
- Store settings: use `findLatestStoreSetting()` / `storeSettingSafeSelect` (avoid unscoped Prisma selects).

## Deploy
- After schema changes: `npx prisma migrate deploy` on production.
- See `docs/FOR_DEVELOPERS.md` and `docs/PROJECT_STRUCTURE.md`.
